  "notes": "{遅刻|ちこく} means arriving after the scheduled or expected time. Functions as both a noun and a suru verb.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{遅刻|ちこく}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to be late for ~\n- {遅刻|ちこく}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{理由|りゆう}→理由：01102_riyuu⟧: reason for being late\n- {遅刻|ちこく}⟦{届|とどけ}→届け：07558_todoke⟧: late arrival notice (at school/work)\n- {遅刻|ちこく}⟦{常習|じょうしゅう}→常習：28124_joushuu⟧: habitual lateness\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nPunctuality is highly valued in Japan. Being late ({遅刻|ちこく}) — even by a few minutes — is taken seriously at school and in the workplace. An apology or explanation is typically expected.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{遅|おく}れる→遅れる：00741_okureru⟧: to be late/delayed (more general — can apply to trains, deliveries, etc.)\n- {遅刻|ちこく}: specifically a person arriving late for a scheduled event",
